1. Clearing Session Lifecycle (clearing_session.session_status)
OPEN: Active clearing business day initiated via BOD. All transactions, uploads, repairs, and verifications are permitted.

CLOSED: Day closed via EOD. Modifications and new batch uploads are locked until the next session is initialized.

2. Staging Pipeline (scan_batch.batch_status & scan_cheque.status)

This stage handles physical image capture and raw scanner ingestion:
RAW: Raw TIFF/JPEG images and raw codeline text received from the scanner.
REJECTED: Batch not validated
STAGED: Batch successfully validated and ready to be transferred to the active clearing tables (outward_batch / outward_cheque).

3. Outward Clearing Cycle (outward_cheque.cheque_status)
Cheques presented by your bank’s customers to be collected from other banks:

PENDING_REPAIR: Codeline is missing or partially unreadable (MICR reject, sort code mismatch, trans code error). Awaiting Maker fix in the MICR Repair Queue.

PENDING_DATA_ENTRY: MICR is valid, but the physical amount, account number, or payee details must be keyed in or balanced against the batch slip.

PENDING_VERIFICATION: Maker has completed entry and balancing; item is waiting for Checker approval.

REJECTED_BY_CHECKER: Checker rejected the cheque .

SENT_BACK_MAKER: returned it to the Maker queue for corrections.

PROCESSED: Verified and approved by the Checker. Ready for clearing file generation.

FILE_GENERATED: Included in the outward clearing presentation file (e.g., CPH / XML) sent to the Clearing House / Central Bank.

CLEARED : The drawee bank accepted the cheque and funds were successfully settled.

UNPROCESSED: The cheque was left in an unfinished pending stage when the Admin executed a Forced EOD.